     2	
     3	Authority: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` (level ladder); owner direction 23 Oct ("verify the sources").
     4	
     5	**Outcome.** The level on the map is real and dated: a dead origin shows L0, a reachable one L1,
     6	a dataset whose files were hashed and whose licence text was captured shows L2, and every level
     7	shows the date it was established.
     8	
     9	**Context today (verified 23 Oct).** `src/osd/verify.py` implements L1 with an injected fetcher,
    10	a single GET with a 1-byte range and a 20 s timeout, and writes `build/verification/<id>.json`
    11	against `schema/verification.schema.json`. L2 checks are declared with outcome `skip`. The
    12	`verify` workflow runs on records PRs and on dispatch and uploads an artifact; the published site
    13	reads the `verification-results` branch (OSD-D5). The SEG wiki and NOPIMS
    14	refuse the VPS with 403 (OSD-D9); five of nine origins answered on 23 Oct.
    15	
    16	**The design the lane must map to.**
    17	1. Reachability classes, closed: `ok` (2xx/3xx), `blocked` (403 or a challenge page body: not
    18	   dead, level stays L1 with detail "blocked from this runner"), `dead` (404/410/DNS failure/
    19	   timeout after one retry), `moved` (final URL host differs: pass with a `known_issues` hint).
    20	2. L2 file check: for records with `origin.manifest_url`, fetch the listing, pick files by a
    21	   per-record `files:` allow-list in a new optional record field `verification.sample`, stream
    22	   each with SHA-256, store `files[]`. Full-dataset hashing is never attempted over 2 GB per run.
    23	3. L2 licence check: fetch `licence.url`, store `licence_text_sha256`; a change in the hash
    24	   between runs is a finding (detail "licence text changed since <date>"), not a failure.
    25	4. Results store: the `verification-results` branch (OSD-D5), written by the verify workflow on
    26	   dispatch and read by pages; the lane keeps that contract and adds nothing else.
    27	5. Freshness: `checked_at` older than 30 days is rendered by the site as "stale" (E05 reads it;
    28	   this lane emits it).
    29	6. Rate: one request per origin at a time, a 2 s pause per host, a fixed User-Agent that names
    30	   the repository.
